<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anak Tomb No. 3</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/357">357</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anak Tomb No. 3 is a painted tomb near Anak in South Hwanghae Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>, dated by an ink inscription to 357 CE. Its murals show its owner, probably Dong Shou, a refugee official from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, with his wife, attendants, a kitchen and a great procession of soldiers. It is one of the earliest and largest Goguryeo-period tombs and part of the UNESCO-listed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/complex-of-koguryo-tombs">Complex of Koguryo Tombs</a>.</p></div>
